---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { href, packages } from "../lib";
---

<Base
  title="Pricing"
  description="Every Leat Consulting package has a fixed scope and a fixed price, agreed in writing before work starts, and ends with a handover."
>
  <h1>Pricing</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Every package has a fixed scope and a fixed price, agreed in writing before any work starts. You
    know what you will receive and what it will cost, and the work ends with a handover.
  </p>

  <ul class="cards">
    {packages.map((p) => (
      <li class="card">
        <h2><a href={href(p.path)}>{p.name}</a></h2>
        <p>{p.summary}</p>
        <p class="small"><strong>You receive:</strong> {p.receive}</p>
        <p><strong>Price on request</strong></p>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <p>
    The price depends on the size of your estate: how many repositories, pipelines and cloud accounts
    are in scope. We agree that list with you first, so the price does not move afterwards.
  </p>
  <p>For AI code review, model usage is billed by Anthropic to your own account, so you always see and control that cost.</p>
  <p class="cta"><a class="button" href={href("contact/")}>Ask for a quote</a></p>
</Base>
